I think it is a bit tedious and sort of an allowed way to cheat. It is
extremely easy to get the exact price of an item, if your not a
tourist. Drop the item twice, first without wearing a shirt or
duncecap and the second time wearing it. Two different prices that 
let you exactly pinpoint the real value.

If you're a tourist or have none of the price reducing armor you just
have to try to sell an item a few times. After a few tries the -1/4
bonus will kick in and again, you have two different prices.

My main complaint is that this approach is foolproof. There is almost
no possibility to screw this up. Compare it to engraving wands. There
is the possibility to engrave with a bad wand(create monsters),
several wands with the same message and some wands that give nothing
away.

Maybe the -1/4 bonus should disappear or the shop keeper should
remember what price he offered for a given item.

